{"title":"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems\">2002 AMC 12B #11</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems\">2002 AMC 10B #15</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/2234a4fad9968f2e6a70981c44d65222d3df15df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, A-B,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> are all prime numbers. The sum of these four primes is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/1279c3decdb0198f652e3856c4ad462a06997970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\mathrm{even} \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\mathrm{divisible\\ by\\ }3 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\mathrm{divisible\\ by\\ }5 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\mathrm{divisible\\ by\\ }7 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\mathrm{prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"692\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6d5a5848db0c94aa754588536b1b218cb81200a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-B$\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> must have the same <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parity\" title=\"Parity\">parity</a>, and since there is only one even prime number, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6d5a5848db0c94aa754588536b1b218cb81200a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-B$\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> are both odd. Thus one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> is odd and the other even. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456d871dc0edb7025eb151497a00bb3cdf4e366d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B &gt; A &gt; A-B &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"196\" height=\"14\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> (as a prime greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) is odd. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed45766ae06d282b582b4b49d4289dcc81331314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbea4cf794ae9ce2d727b26f3a3c4246e8e47601.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-2, A, A+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" /> are consecutive odd primes. At least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbea4cf794ae9ce2d727b26f3a3c4246e8e47601.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-2, A, A+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, from which it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d2c2236d016f37c0b87b01d4991f187c58e8154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-2 = 3$\" width=\"77\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/a/14a7b7cfba975b9ef5efff26ae652dd4b2d9ef5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 5$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. The sum of these numbers is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, a prime, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f06a4001910549904e9688da5a96dd125a7a49c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\text{prime}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"85\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order for both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e589efce2b099b83a8437a41f75acdce0c8e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A - B$\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> to be prime, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef747a48a2a8d43c4841e12c89f2de2502a672e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> must be 2, or else both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e589efce2b099b83a8437a41f75acdce0c8e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A - B$\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> would be even numbers. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1c13d77e2b5ede10a622c2229043191de82ce17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 2$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4daec1b65b2c7204eba605d45b19b072005b0218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &lt; B$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/12264f41330c32dcd66cd377031cbdb5f48ea9a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A - B &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />, which is not possible. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed45766ae06d282b582b4b49d4289dcc81331314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/263cea2ba72385dfcb2f0a867ab2015643b8cfca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &gt; A - B &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"121\" height=\"13\" />, we can infer that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/43774152564421c2e7784fb38e533693aa22b400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/78525cbaa7d3414f24edec96d599421309313c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6n \\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> for some natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>However in either case, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e589efce2b099b83a8437a41f75acdce0c8e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A - B$\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bf77c6740d00af2866f26718d628a60c667ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/975b181b463919f2ce32ac1b617d7e261f8a98ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6n \\pm 3 = 3(2n \\pm 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" /> which is a multiple of 3. Therefore the only possibility that works is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/e/1aef9950a3d23f38e0044c835a680795e1021141.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A - B = 3$\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009d79e62fcb86d45c7d973d181b0c3b8d45bb69.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A + B + (A - B) + (A + B) = 5 + 2 + 3 + 7 = 17\\]\" width=\"393\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Which is a prime number. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0cd82367e63fe9f487758f5656e94818f4d4b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~ Nafer\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(intuitive)\">Solution 3 (intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (intuitive)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Trying out some primes for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6d5a5848db0c94aa754588536b1b218cb81200a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-B$\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> are prime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d72c739bd8c2b60ef756afaf71e48afd30a74938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=5$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/3417d76d7ccdf011b0760de58dd37e42a924bdf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> can be found almost immediately. Summing the four primes, the result is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/8/1e80b2d536a8c1b29682865928ed0ff101b3a6d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+2+3+7=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f06a4001910549904e9688da5a96dd125a7a49c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\text{prime}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"85\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B\">2002 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\"